    fix(cli): validate --format json emits every spec report and prints no banner on stdout (DF-SPECLANG-9)
    
    Two defects from dogfood, both reproduced here before the change:
    
    1. A spec that fails to PARSE was dropped from `.reports[]` while the run
       exited 1 — `totalFiles` said 2, `reports` had 1, and the array held zero
       errors, so a machine consumer counting reports saw a clean run.
       `validateCommand`'s catch block only incremented `totalErrors`; it now
       pushes a `parseFailureReport()` entry for the file (rule
       `@validation/parse`, level error, message carrying the parse error) so
       reports.length === totalFiles in every outcome.
    
    2. The human banner "📋 Validating specs..." was printed to STDOUT before the
       JSON payload, so `speclang validate --format json | jq .` could not parse.
       `--format json` now routes the banner (and `check`'s "🔍 Checking specs...")
       to STDERR; text mode is unchanged.
    
    Also fixes the same stdout-purity class in `check --format json`.
    
    Evidence (this worktree):
    - pre-fix fixture (2 spec files, one unparsable): totalFiles=2,
      reports=1, reports-with-errors=0, rc=1, stdout began "📋 Validat..."
    - post-fix same fixture: reports=2, reports-with-errors=1, rc=1,
      stdout begins "{" and parses with jq
    - real repo: 452 spec files (450 *.spec.md + 2 *.scl) -> reports=452,
      totalFiles=452, rc=0. The NASA playbook spec that used to fail now
      parses (fixed in ebdfe1be, README-18), so the in-tree error count is 0;
      the drop defect is pinned by the new fixture test instead.
    - text mode: per-file error still on stderr and exit 1 on the fixture
      (AC3); repo-wide text run exits 0 because no spec currently fails.
    
    Tests: tests/cli.test.ts "validate --format json report integrity" — asserts
    stdout parses with plain JSON.parse (no banner-tolerant helper), report count
    equals spec file count, the failing spec is present with its error, exit 1,
    and the text-mode stderr path. Verified RED against the pre-fix tree
    (SyntaxError: "📋 Validat..." is not valid JSON) and green after.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
